{
  "destination": {
    "name": "Khulna",
    "country": "Bangladesh",
    "latitude": 22.8456,
    "longitude": 89.5403,
    "description": "Khulna (খুলনা Khulnā) is the third largest city of Bangladesh. It is the administrative capital city of Khulna Division in Southern Bangladesh. On the bank of Rupsha and Bhoirob river. It is renowned as an industrial city and a river port city. It is also the third most populous city in the country. It is known in Bangladesh for its economic importance and for The Sunderbans. Khulna is the gateway city of the Sundarbans which is the largest mangrove forest in the world."
