      "latitude": 22.674604,
      "longitude": 89.741993,
      "description": "200px|thumb|right|The Shait Gumbad MosqueLiterally meaning the \"Mosque of 60 domes\", it's slightly misnamed as it actually has 77. It was built in 1549, and is one of the country's best mosques. While it's not un-interesting, if you've seen any mosque in India, Pakistan, Iran, or Afghanistan from this period you'll be pretty underwhelmed. Worse is that foreigners are charged to see the mosque…",
